Z||000017||theogre||09-29-2000||02:26 PM||||The best way to put diferant color sheets behind a lense is to use theatric lighting gels. Gel sheet will take the heat buildup better and hold it's color longer. The stuff comes in literally hundreds of shades and colors. You can get it at the stage supply houses in any big city. You can probably mail order the stuff. The smallest it comes is about a 2 foot square sheet. It's not cheap.||||reg||1
